From 3d6d22167823f30419140f058cdaed49b3f7bdd0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:09:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): a block that waits on time parks scheduled with
 a wake, not as a human block [daveey]

Goal-mode cards may not call kanban_schedule, so workers waiting on a clock
(a nightly run, a soak, a release) used kanban_block(kind=dependency).
With no open parent the kernel re-kinded that to needs_input, the card sat
in blocked, and the Desktop sidebar painted its chat red as needing a human.

- block_task: kind='time' (new), a parent-less dependency, or a reason with
  SCHEDULED_UNTIL=<ISO8601> parks the card 'scheduled' with a wake time on
  its scheduled event (default 24h, clamp 14d) via hermes_cli/kanban_timed_park.
  A parent-less dependency behind a shared blocker_id keeps the sticky
  needs_input rekind.
- wake_due_continuations honours scheduled events that carry wake_at, so a
  kanban_schedule SCHEDULED_UNTIL marker is now a real timer.
- Sidebar counts (kanban_session_activity): kanban_blocked counts only
  human blocks (needs_input/capability/untyped); transient/time blocks count
  as in-progress work.
- kanban_block schema + KANBAN_GUIDANCE name kind='time' for goal-mode cards.
